{"name":"Pink Champagne","hex":"#e8dfed","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"pink","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A color reminiscent of pinks, the flowers.","Magenta, the colour evoked by red and blue light when combined."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a colour between red and white; pale red.","Of a fox-hunter's jacket: scarlet."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/pink"},{"term":"champagne","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sparkling white wine made from a blend of grapes, especially Chardonnay and pinot, produced in Champagne, France, by the méthode champenoise.","Any sparkling wine made by the méthode champenoise."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a very pale brownish-gold colour, similar to that of champagne.","Alternative form of champaine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/champagne"}],"entries":[{"title":"Pink Champagne","blocks":[{"text":"Pink Champagne was a Swedish feminist punk band in the 1980s. It consisted of four women, Stina Berge (drums), Ann Carlberger (vocals), Karin Jansson (guitar) and Gunilla Welin (bass). Kajsa Grytt was briefly a member. They released two full-length albums, Vackra pojke! and Kärlek eller ingenting, before breaking up in 1984."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink_Champagne","wikidata":"Q7195978"},{"title":"Pink Champagne (E-girls song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Pink Champagne\" is a song recorded and performed by Japanese collective unit E-girls, taken as a single from their fourth studio album E.G. Crazy (2017). The track was released on August 10, 2016 through Rhythm Zone and Avex Music Creative Inc. in three physical formats—two CD's and a DVD bundle—and for digital consumption. The song was written by Masoto Kotake and produced by Exile Hiro. Additionally, each addition apart from the one-track format came with the two B-sides: \"Bad Girls\" and \"Cowgirl Rhapsody\" which was produced by Skylar Mones, one remix of their single \"Dance Dance Dance\" and the first three instrumental tracks, respectively."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f7/Egirlspinkchampagnecdonly.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink_Champagne_(E-girls_song)","wikidata":"Q24873328"},{"title":"Champagne","blocks":[{"text":"Champagne is a sparkling wine originated and produced in the Champagne wine region of France under the AOC rules of the appellation, which demand specific vineyard practices, sourcing of grapes exclusively from designated places within it, specific grape-pressing methods and secondary fermentation of the wine in the bottle to cause carbonation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Glass_of_champagne.jpg/330px-Glass_of_champagne.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Champagne","wikidata":"Q134862"},{"title":"Pink","blocks":[{"text":"Pink is a pale tint of red or rose, the color of the pink flower. It was first used as a color name in the late 17th century. A combination of pink and white is associated with innocence, whereas a combination of pink and black links to eroticism and seduction."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg/330px-Pink_sapphire_ring.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pink","wikidata":"Q429220"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/A_village_with_vineyards_in_Champagne%2C_France_1987.jpg/500px-A_village_with_vineyards_in_Champagne%2C_France_1987.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/A_village_with_vineyards_in_Champagne%2C_France_1987.jpg/1280px-A_village_with_vineyards_in_Champagne%2C_France_1987.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/A_village_with_vineyards_in_Champagne%2C_France_1987.jpg/500px-A_village_with_vineyards_in_Champagne%2C_France_1987.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Vineyards in the Champagne region of France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_village_with_vineyards_in_Champagne%2C_France_1987.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/De_Troy_Oyster_Lunch.PNG/330px-De_Troy_Oyster_Lunch.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/De_Troy_Oyster_Lunch.PNG/330px-De_Troy_Oyster_Lunch.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Jean François de Troy's 1735 painting Le Déjeuner d'Huîtres (The Oyster Luncheon) is the first known depiction of Champagne in painting.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADe_Troy_Oyster_Lunch.PNG"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b8/Anbau_champagner.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b8/Anbau_champagner.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"A map of French wine regions, with the Champagne appellation highlighted in red","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnbau_champagner.png"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1f/Grape-Shot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1f/Grape-Shot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"1915 English magazine illustration of a lady riding a Champagne cork (Lordprice Collection)","link":"ht